From efa7f2723d0eebeafd313a534102bc637f3119aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:52:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/19] accel/ane, media: apple: ave: T6050 Neural Engine on
 macOS 27.3; AVE builds by TEXT CRC

The T6050 ANE driver admits one preloaded firmware build, the macOS 27.0
one. Give it a table of admitted builds and let the handed-off layout
select the build. ANE: 27.0 TEXT 0xc0000 and DATA 0x2ac000 at DVA
0x100000c0000; 27.3 (26C5035r) TEXT 0xec000 and DATA 0x280000 at
0x100000ec000, each with its own TEXT sha256 pin. The H17 backend sizes its
IPC from the firmware boot request (27.3 asks 0x10441 bytes) instead of a
fixed 0xc441, and ane_t6021.boot_stages=N holds the bind after N bring-up
stages.

AVE: #1747 admits the 27.3 (26C5035r) build by its segment sizes. Builds
may share sizes (27.2 26B123 has 27.3's), so let the TEXT CRC, with the
sizes, select the build. apple_ave.ave_t6050_27_3_hevc=0 refuses HEVC on
the 27.3 build.

Ported from betizzel/omarchy-m5 patches/upstream-27.3/0004; rebased onto
integration/aurora a34d26c2 (after #1747).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
